    "result_text": "The suite is green. There's exactly one test class (`AcceptanceTest`; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `telephoneDisplay` field to the owner response that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans, while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits it into `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/TelephoneDisplays.java`** (new) \u2014 Formatter that turns E.164 (`+61412345678`) into display form (`+61 412 345 678`): splits off the country code (recognizing the same `61`/`1` codes the E.164 normalizer knows, longest-prefix-first), then groups the national digits in threes. It returns the raw value unchanged for anything not in `+`-then-digits form, matching the `Localities`-style utility convention already in the codebase.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression populating `telephoneDisplay` from `TelephoneDisplays.displayFor(owner)`, alongside the other derived fields.\n\nThe `telephone` field is untouched \u2014 it stays the raw E.164 value produced by the existing `OwnerTelephone.toE164` normalizer.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (input `0412 345 678` \u2192 `telephone` `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` `+61 412 345 678`) passes, and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
